  "body": "Introduced by #84's fix (drill_reach.rs). Drilling has no record of what earlier operations removed, so with a setup stock declared it measures hole depth from the stock top (capped at the R plane) down - a hole on the floor of an already-machined pocket reads as the pocket depth plus the hole depth and is refused when that exceeds the flute, although the material above the floor is gone. Fails safe (a refusal, never a silent collision), but valid programs are refused.\n\nDone means: the reach check reads the in-process stock left by the earlier operations of the setup (the rest-material / stock simulation the app already has), or measures from the part surface plus the rest stock above the hole; pinned by a pocket-then-drill test that posts, and a drill-first test that still refuses.",
